What does clairvoyence (the spell) do?

______________________________________________________________
	I walk boldly down the dungeon corridor. Just having 
stumbled down a set of slippery hewn steps I am a little nervous.
The entrance to the winding case of steps was hard to find
and I almost got caught in a nasty looking rusty metal trap
in my glee to start into the steep blackish tunnel.
	It finally came to a narrow opening and into
a wider, more used, and level hallyway. That is what is
making me nervous. Why would anyone set a trap infront of
a dangerous stairway unless there was something important
below. And now this place looks used. I have my trusty sword
in hand and my loyal, but I am afraid hungry, cat is tagging
at my heels. Hex seems to sense no danger so I am feeling 
ok. 
	I hear a creaking in the distance, and some grating of
a stone door being opened and closed. Who ever it is is close.
I try and tread softy.
I round a slow corner and see the back of a nasty greenish looking
creature hunched over the lock of a door clicking something!
I prepare to charge, but it spins around and looks at me disarmingly.
It is a friendly creature. 
	My cat however has a differnt idea in mind and leaps upon it.
I don't have a leash so there is nothing I can do. I poor thing is
wrecked and dies quickly. Hex begins to eat. I pick up the
long thin peice of metal the creature was using on the door. Perhaps it
will help with the banded metal chest back up the stairs.
	 
	
